      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In the peripheral blood from 15 patients with coronary heart disease and from 18 with arrhythmias the parameters of peroxidic lipid oxidation were estimated by means of a chemiluminescence method. From the data obtained we conclude that any patient has an individual sensitivity to hyperbaric oxygen. The confidential intervals of the \"index of chemiluminescence ICh\" were determined both for the ischemic and the arrhythmic group. In both of them there were patients with positive and negative responses to the hyperbaric oxygen treatment. We observed that in the subgroups characteristic fluctuations of the confidential bounds may occur. The easy assessment of parameters of peroxidic lipid oxidation under hyperbaric oxygenation allows to predict the effectivity of the treatment and to control its timing."},
